    <div class="modal-body">
      <!-- Question recap -->
      <div class="ans-question-box">
        <div class="ans-q-title">How do I derive the quadratic formula from ax² + bx + c = 0 by completing the square?</div>
        <div class="ans-q-desc">I understand the formula itself but I'm confused about the "completing the square" method used to derive it. My textbook skips steps between isolating x² and getting the final ±√(b²−4ac)/2a.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:.45rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <span class="tag-subj s-math">#Mathematics</span>
          <span class="tag-misc">#algebra</span>
          <span class="tag-misc">#quadratic</span>
          <span class="tag-misc">#class-12</span>
        </div>
      </div>

